===Glyph origin===
{{Han etyl}}
{{liushu|p}} – alternative interpretation, either an arm bending out from the side of the body, or a wooden plough. The original version was 𠠲 and the letter ㄌ in zhuyin alphabet was inspired by this character.

See also the original version of [[爭]], in which another plow can be seen. Unrelated to [[工]] and perhaps to [[耒]] since they are two different tools. Also unrelated to [[另]].

===Etymology===
From {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*k-ra||strength; to win; classifier for people}} + ''*-k'' (STEDT; {{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}). Cognate with {{cog|my|အား||strength; force}}; {{cog|tbq-lol-pro|*ra²||strength}}, whence {{cog|ii|ꊋ}}; {{cog|bfc|tr=ɣɯ̱⁴²|t=strength}}; {{cog|bca|hhep||strength}}. A causative derivative is {{och-l|飭|tr=rhək}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).

{{zh-ref|Schuessler (2007)}} also suggests an etymological connection with {{och-l|來|to come}}.

